.TH AVR\-ORG\-INSTALL\-SET\-SELECTION 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-install-set-selection \- Replace a GitLab installation's project selection.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org install set-selection
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace a GitLab installation's project selection.
.PP
Use `--project-selection selected` without `--project-id` to select no projects. This updates the selection only; the next project sync applies it.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    access_token_expires_on, access_token_invalid_at,
    access_token_last_validated_at, created_at, credential_kind,
    gitlab_namespace_full_path, gitlab_namespace_id, gitlab_project_ids,
    installation_id, organization_id, project_selection_mode, configured_runner_count,
    degraded_runner_count, selected_project_count, state, target_type,
    updated_at, webhook_secret_rotated_at
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-installation\-id\fR \fITEXT\fR
GitLab installation ID (ins-xxx format). (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-selection\fR \fICHOICE\fR
Project selection mode. (choices: all, selected; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-project\-id\fR \fIINTEGER RANGE\fR
GitLab numeric project ID to select (repeatable, up to 1,000). (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
